Hello,

As you know, the great service at nethack.alt.org allows to watch games
in progress, in real time. Unfortunately, this functionality is not
available on devnull tournament servers. Some folks from the Cabal clan
tried to improve this situation. Hence, the new service, termcast. From
the service homepage at http://noway.ratry.ru/jsn/termcast/ :

What is it?

It's a service for watching/broadcasting live terminal sessions (like
NetHack games, or, in fact, any other console-based game or other
terminal activity).

How can I watch the games?

Just connect to noway.ratry.ru, port 37331 using your telnet client of
choice. If you use Windows (tm), it's probably putty. Unix/Linux users
can just run "telnet noway.ratry.ru 37331".

How can I make my game available for watching?

You need to download `ttyrec' utility, to record your games, and
`ttrtail' utility, to stream your game record to the server in real
time. Sources for both are available from the service homepage, should
work out of the box on unix; Windows/cygwin binaries are also available
(you'll need cygwin to run those, though).

More information is available from http://noway.ratry.ru/jsn/termcast/

good luck,
-jsn.



